## Tools

The following tools were used to conduct the experiments and evaluate test effectiveness:

### Test Generation
- **Large Language Models (LLMs)**  
  Used to automatically generate unit test cases for selected benchmark classes.

### Benchmark Dataset
- **Defects4J**  
  A standardized dataset of real-world Java bugs and human-written test suites used as the baseline for comparison.

### Coverage Analysis
- **JaCoCo**  
  Java code coverage library used to measure line coverage and determine how much of the code is executed by each test suite.

### Mutation Testing
- **PIT (Pitest)**  
  Mutation testing tool used to evaluate fault detection by injecting small faults (mutants) into the code and measuring how many are detected by the tests.

### Build & Execution
- **Maven**  
  Used to compile projects, run tests, and integrate JaCoCo and PIT into the workflow.

### Development Environment
- **IntelliJ IDEA**  
  Used for running experiments, configuring plugins, and analyzing reports.
